## Phaser-Specific Implementation Approaches

### 1. Container-Based Composition

Using Phaser's Container as a base class provides the best flexibility for component-based entities:

```typescript
// The container holds visual elements and components
const enemy = new PhaserEntity(scene, x, y);
const sprite = scene.add.sprite(0, 0, 'enemy');
enemy.add(sprite);

// Adding components that can work with any container-based entity
enemy.addComponent('health', new HealthComponent(enemy, 100));
enemy.addComponent('movement', new MovementComponent(enemy, 150));
```

### 2. Extended GameObject Approach

For simpler entities, extending Phaser GameObjects and adding component functionality:

```typescript
class ComponentGameObject extends Phaser.GameObjects.Sprite {
  private components: Map<string, Component> = new Map();
  
  // Component methods...
  
  update(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Update components
    this.components.forEach(component => component.update(time, delta));
  }
}
```

### 3. Mixins for Feature Composition

Using TypeScript mixins to compose features into Phaser objects:

```typescript
// Define a mixin that adds health functionality
function withHealth<T extends Constructor<Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject>>(Base: T) {
  return class extends Base {
    private health: number = 100;
    
    takeDamage(amount: number): void {
      this.health -= amount;
      // Damage logic...
    }
    
    heal(amount: number): void {
      this.health += amount;
      // Healing logic...
    }
  };
}

// Create a class with the mixin
const PlayerSprite = withHealth(Phaser.GameObjects.Sprite);
const player = new PlayerSprite(scene, x, y, 'player');
```

### 4. Scene-Level Component Managers

For performance-critical systems, using scene-level managers:

```typescript
class PhysicsManager {
  private scene: Phaser.Scene;
  private entities: Map<string, PhysicsData> = new Map();
  
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    this.scene = scene;
    scene.events.on('update', this.update, this);
  }
  
  register(id: string, entity: Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject, config: PhysicsConfig): void {
    // Setup physics for entity
  }
  
  update(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Update all registered entities' physics
  }
}
```

### 5. Proper Event Handling

Always clean up event listeners to prevent memory leaks:

```typescript
// In your component or entity class
private events: Array<{emitter: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, listener: Function}> = [];

// Register event with tracking
addEvent(emitter: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, listener: Function): void {
  emitter.on(event, listener, this);
  this.events.push({ emitter, event, listener });
}

// Cleanup on destroy
destroy(): void {
  this.events.forEach(({ emitter, event, listener }) => {
    emitter.off(event, listener, this);
  });
  this.events = [];
}
```

